# sweep: --seed-root examples/books/fixtures/chapters
# Go to, on The Lock Keeper's Year. The controls say the place beside the way
# to change it. The stepper moves a tenth of the book at a tap and names the
# page it comes to, a page can be typed on the digits instead, and Back, or
# the control that names the page that was left, returns to it.
wait-for Lock Keeper
tap The Lock Keeper
wait-for Spring
tap-id reader-controls
wait-for Page 1 of 8
expect Go to
shot books-goto-controls
tap Go to
wait-for You are on page 1 of 8.
expect Go to page 1
shot books-goto
tap-id reader-go-to-more
wait-for 10%
tap-id reader-go-to-more
tap-id reader-go-to-more
tap-id reader-go-to-more
tap-id reader-go-to-more
wait-for 50%
expect Go to page 5
shot books-goto-stepped
tap Go to page 5
wait-for Autumn
expect-missing You are on page
# The controls name the page that was left, and go back to it.
tap-id reader-controls
wait-for Page 5 of 8
expect Back to page 1
shot books-goto-return
tap Back to page 1
wait-for Spring
tap-id reader-controls
wait-for Page 1 of 8
expect-missing Back to page
# A typed page: one the book does not have is said not to be one, and one it
# has is turned to.
tap Go to
wait-for You are on page 1 of 8.
tap Type a page
wait-for-id kb.enter
expect A number from 1 to 8.
shot books-goto-type
type 99
tap-id kb.enter
wait-for The pages run from 1 to 8.
shot books-goto-refused
tap Type a page
wait-for-id kb.enter
type 7
tap-id kb.enter
wait-for Winter
# Back from the page returns to the one that was left.
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for Spring
expect-missing Continue reading
